WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.387
Sometimes the goal is to build one readable field from several columns.

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:08.562
CONCAT_WS means concatenate with separator.

00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:17.247
It is especially useful when some components can be NULL because it avoids producing unnecessary separators

00:00:17.247 --> 00:00:21.522
for missing arguments. NULLIF can convert an empty string to NULL first.

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:26.707
That combination helps create clean display lines without confusing blanks.

00:00:26.707 --> 00:00:32.962
Connect this idea to a CRM standardizing names, emails, and phone numbers.

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:38.687
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.687 --> 00:00:46.522
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:52.462
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:52.462 --> 00:00:58.480
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
